    "bio": "Joi Cardwell is an American singer and songwriter. Born and raised in New York City, she performed in various singing competitions as a child and rose to fame in the early 1990s as a guest vocalist for Lil Louis on the number-one Dance singles \"Club Lonely\" and \"Saved My Life\". The release of Cardwell's debut album, The World Is Full of Trouble (1995), established her as a solo artist and featured the US top-five Dance Club Songs \"Jump for Joi\" and \"Love & Devotion\". Her second album, Joi Cardwell (1997), produced top-charting singles \"Soul to Bare\", \"Run to You\", and \"Found Love\".",
