    "raw_title": "LeToya Luckett",
    "qid": "Q257302",
    "bio": "LeToya Nicole Luckett-Coles is an American R&B singer and actress. She rose to fame in the late 1990s as a founding member of the R&B girl group Destiny's Child, one of the world's best-selling girl groups of all time. As a member of Destiny's Child, she achieved four US Top 10 hit singles, \"No, No, No\", \"Bills, Bills, Bills\", \"Jumpin', Jumpin'\", and\n\"Say My Name\", sold over 25 million records, and won two Grammy Awards. In the 2000s, she began her solo career after leaving the group and signing a record deal with Capitol Records.",
