    "bio": "Philippé Wynne was an American singer, best known for his role as a lead vocalist of The Spinners. Wynne scored notable hits such as \"How Could I Let You Get Away\", \"The Rubberband Man\", and \"One of a Kind \". After leaving The Spinners, Wynne never regained the same success, although he was featured in hits by other artists such as \"(Not Just) Knee Deep\" by Funkadelic. Wynne died of a heart attack while performing at a nightclub.",
